<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petar II Petrović-Njegoš</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1813–1851</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Njegoš</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Petar II Petrović-Njegoš was prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Montenegro from 1830 to 1851 and one of the great poets of the South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a>. He created a senate, introduced taxes and strengthened central rule over the clans, and he wrote the verse drama <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-mountain-wreath">The Mountain Wreath</a>. His mausoleum stands on Mount Lovćen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petar-ii-petrovic-njegos.jpg" alt="Petar II Petrović-Njegoš" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Böss · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Petar_II_Petrovi%C4%87-Njego%C5%A1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
